---
description: Investigate PokeFarm runs and fix what makes them fail — pull the actionable failure queue over the pokepilot MCP, replay the failing round's .state locally, fix at the shared point, commit and push once the tests pass.
globs:
alwaysApply: false
---

Follow the procedure in @.claude/skills/pokefarm-triage/SKILL.md exactly. It is
the single source of truth for this workflow; this rule only makes Cursor aware
of it.

The short version, so you know what you are opting into:

1. Start with `pokepilot_get_triage()`. It is the actionable queue and hides
   linked issues already marked resolved/fixed. Use `include_resolved=true`
   only to audit history. `pokepilot_list_runs` is raw evidence, not a backlog;
   never recreate work just by grouping old `detail` strings.
2. `pokepilot_get_run_debug(run_id)` for `trace_tail`, `progress_final`, and the
   artifact list.
3. `curl` the failing round's `.state` artifact from the pokewall endpoint.
4. Replay it in a throwaway `skill/zz_repro_scratch_test.go` before editing
   anything — the farm runs committed HEAD, so a farm failure reproduces
   locally in seconds and deterministically.
5. Fix where every caller routes through, not on the path the failure named.
6. Gate on `make test-short` (~6s) plus the repro. Never run the bare
   `go test ./skill/...`: those tests boot the emulator and play the game for
   tens of minutes.
7. Branch, commit the fix only, push. Leave unrelated dirty files unstaged.
